# ── Secrets scaffold (EXAMPLE — copy to a real secrets source, NEVER commit the real one) ──
# .gitignore excludes *.env except *.example.env. In real deployment these are populated
# from a secrets manager / mounted file, not this file. See internal/secrets/secrets.go.

# Door 3 — the global HMAC email-hash pepper. THE MOST FRAGILE SECRET IN THE SYSTEM.
# Generated ONCE with strong entropy; stored OUTSIDE the DB; redundant, geo-separate,
# access-audited backups; recovery DRILLED before P1 ships; rotation additive-only.
# Losing it de-joins ALL history forever; leaking it makes addresses brute-forceable.
# (Example value below is NOT a real pepper — generate your own, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.)
TM_PEPPER=REPLACE_WITH_32_BYTES_OF_ENTROPY_never_this_placeholder

# The service-role key gating ALL state. DDL/grant-admin is a SEPARATE break-glass cred
# (PN-9 / DR-3), not this one.
TM_SUPABASE_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY

# Caller -> control-plane bearer. Accepted on the SYNC /v1/verify during transition; the P5 bulk
# surface (/v1/verify/bulk) REQUIRES a per-caller key (PN-13 / §3.8) — see api_callers.
TM_FRONTDOOR_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_FRONT_DOOR_BEARER

# P5 DR-4 (ADR-0002) — at-rest encryption key for the work_items plaintext-address column (the ONE
# bounded Door-3 exception). A SEPARATE secret from the pepper, DELIBERATELY (F-9/F-19): never
# derived from it, never stored with it. Losing THIS key only makes in-flight (not-yet-settled)
# work undecryptable (recoverable — re-enqueue); losing the pepper de-joins ALL history forever.
# Exactly 32 bytes (AES-256) as hex or base64 (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`). The queue subsystem
# refuses to start without it, and /readyz then answers 503 not_ready ("reasons" names this key)
# even if you only ever call the sync /v1/verify: set it on every deployment you want reported ready.
# TM_QUEUE_ADDR_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_32_BYTES_OF_ENTROPY_hex_or_base64
# Previous key during a rotation overlap (optional): decrypt tries current-then-previous so items
# sealed under the old key still open while they re-seal or drain (bounded by max_retry_age).
# TM_QUEUE_ADDR_KEY_PREV=

# control-plane -> verifier-node node tokens: "nodeid=token,nodeid2=token2". Per-node unique (P3 §6.4).
# Referenced by node id from the config node-list; never stored in the nodes table in clear.
TM_NODE_TOKENS=

# control-plane -> vendor keys (P6): "millionverifier=key". Layer stays DISABLED until a key + DPA exist.
TM_VENDOR_KEYS=

# ── Non-secret runtime knobs (safe to set in plain config; shown here for convenience) ──
# TM_ENV=production
# TM_LISTEN_ADDR=:8080
# Postgres/Supabase DSN. Empty => /v1/verify reports not-ready (503); the control-plane still
# serves health/readiness. Holds a password, so treat like a secret (loaded from env, never committed).
# TM_DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/dbname
# Migration runner (cmd/migrate, FW-3) — NOT read by the control plane. The DSN of the MIGRATING identity (a superuser, or Supabase's `postgres`), never the runtime
# verify_app, which has no privilege on the tracker. A direct or session-mode connection (the run holds a session advisory lock). Holds a password: treat like a secret.
# TM_MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:pass@host:5432/dbname
# Directory of NNNN_*.sql the runner reads (default: migrations, relative to the working directory).
# TM_MIGRATIONS_DIR=migrations
# Cache TTL in seconds (P1 OQ-9 — owner DIAL). UNSET => caching is SKIPPED (never a guessed
# expires_at; §4.2 requires it NOT NULL). Set a value to enable the verdict cache.
# TM_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=86400
# Kill-switch ladder (operator can pull a rung by config, no redeploy — Door 5):
# TM_SMTP_MODE=disabled        # enabled|disabled  (P0/P1 default: disabled — no SMTP infra)
# TM_FALLBACK_MODE=off         # enabled|off       (P0/P1 default: off — no vendor)
# TM_FRONTDOOR_MODE=serving    # serving|accept_and_defer|reject
# A single node keeps the LIST shape exercised (Door 5):
# TM_NODE_ID=mock-1
# TM_NODE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# TM_NODE_ENABLED=false
# Phase 2: brain-side deadline on a /v1/verify node call (§6.5). UNSET => 15s client default.
# The P5 lease TTL must EXCEED this (latent numeric coupling). A timeout => unknown/smtp_timeout.
# TM_SMTP_CLIENT_DEADLINE_MS=8000
# SMTP runs only when TM_SMTP_MODE=enabled AND a node is routable; else cheap-layers-only (Rung 3).
# The node token is resolved from TM_NODE_TOKENS (nodeid=token,...), never from config in clear.
